  "baseTranscript": "Can you trust your team to meet real needs on time? More AI output alone does not earn that trust. Just-in-time is the other pillar of the Toyota production system. Only what is needed, when needed, in the amount needed. Minimum stock, dependable flow. Just-in-time entrusts capable people to respond to real need. Be resourceful with what you have. Pull a small customer problem, not a queue of technical tasks. Let one useful end-to-end outcome pull the necessary work. Trust the team and AI. Handle complexity together, resourcefully. Earn trust through quality in a shared working product. Use feedback to choose again. Leave later work unstarted. Integrate small changes continuously. Keep one coherent product. When a dependency becomes real, let it pull collaboration. Technical excellence makes that response dependable. Build the capability to meet real needs, on time.",
